        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The query is saved at `/app/solution.sparql` and verified against the graph with rdflib. It returns:\n\n| professorName | countries |\n|---|---|\n| Aristotle Tympas | GR |\n| Orfeas Menis | GR |\n| Pepe Attanasio | GR |\n\nHow it works:\n- **Full professors**: role starts with \"Professor\" but not \"Assistant Professor\".\n- **EU filter**: `VALUES` list of the 27 EU member-state ISO codes (as of 2025), matched via department → `uni:belongsTo` → university → `uni:locatedInCountry`.\n- **>10 current students**: a subquery counts distinct students per department enrolled in courses taught there whose enrollment date ≤ 2025-08-16 and who have no graduation date or a graduation date after 2025-08-16; `FILTER(?cnt > 10)` plus an equivalent `FILTER EXISTS` ensures at least one of the professor's departments qualifies.\n- Results are grouped by name with `GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?country)`.\n\nSanity check of the data confirms this: ComputerScience_NTUA (CS101, 12 active students) and HistoryAndPhilosophy_NKUA (STS101, 13 active students) qualify, while Mathematics_Sorbonne's Math201 drops below 10 once students who graduated before 2025-08-16 are excluded — hence Marie Dubois is correctly omitted.",
            "session_id": "tb-5a95312a8d"
        }
